# Vercel root-project deployments: upload only what the root build needs.
#
# History: this file previously contained a bare `*` (ignore everything).
# That worked when deploys were made from `website/` as the project root,
# but against the root-project setup (root vercel.json + npm --prefix
# website ...) it uploads a tree with no files at all, so
# `npm --prefix website install` fails with ENOENT (exit 254).
#
# Keep the upload minimal but functional: exclude the heavy media/tooling
# trees and local-only folders, keep everything the build reads.
backend/bin/
backend/test_data/
data/
data-experimental/
docs/ui-checks/
docs/local-experimental/
frontend-app/node_modules/
website/node_modules/
website/.next/
website/.vercel/
mobile-android/build/
mobile-android/.gradle/
